Binary Search :

Binary search is a technique to search in a sorted (or monotonic) space by repeatedly dividing it into halves.
At each step:
Compute mid
Compare with target (or condition)
Eliminate half of the space

int low = 0, high = n - 1;

while (low <= high) {
    int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;

    if (condition == satisfied) {
        return mid;
    } else if (go left) {
        high = mid - 1;
    } else {
        low = mid + 1;
    }
}

Where Binary Search Can Be Used
Classic: Sorted Arrays
Search element
First/last occurrence
Count occurrences
Rotated Sorted Arrays
Search in rotated array
Find minimum (pivot)
Square root
Precision problems (double values)
While reassigning always ensure :

