high = mid - 1;

For a Binary Search Tree (BST) or any Binary Tree, the three fundamental Depth First Search (DFS) traversals are:

Preorder → Root → Left → Right
Inorder → Left → Root → Right
Postorder → Left → Right → Root

1.  Preorder :
void preorder(TreeNode node){
    if(node == null) return;

    visit(node);          // process current node
    preorder(node.left);
    preorder(node.right);
}

When to Use Preorder
1. Copying / Cloning a Tree : You process root first, so structure can be recreated.
2. Serialize Tree : Saving tree structure to file/network.
3. Expression Trees (Prefix Notation)  : + a * b c
4. Building Trees  : Useful when reconstructing BSTs from traversal arrays.

2. Inorder Traversal

void inorder(TreeNode node){
    if(node == null) return;

    inorder(node.left);
    visit(node);
    inorder(node.right);
}

When to Use Inorder
1. Get Sorted Data from BST :
2. Validate BST
3. kth Smallest / Largest Element
4. Range Queries
5. Convert BST → Sorted Array / LinkedList


3. Postorder Traversal

void postorder(TreeNode node){
    if(node == null) return;

    postorder(node.left);
    postorder(node.right);
    visit(node);
}

