When to Use Postorder:
1. Delete/Free Tree : Children must be deleted before parent.
2. Expression Tree Evaluation : Operands evaluated before operator.
3. Bottom-Up Processing : When child results are needed before parent.
4. Calculate Heights / Sizes : Dynamic programming on trees.
5. Dependency Resolution :  Children/dependencies processed first.

| Traversal | Process Node     |
| --------- | ---------------- |
| Preorder  | Before children  |
| Inorder   | Between children |
| Postorder | After children   |


